   "subject": "Re: items desperatly ordered alphabetically with Geom_bar despite stat=identity",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Alchiba,\r<br>\r<br>Try:\r<br>\r<br>df1$chr &lt;- factor(df1$chr, levels = c(as.character(1:22), &quot;X&quot;, &quot;Y&quot;, &quot;MT&quot;))\r<br>ggplot(df1, aes(chr, count)) + geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>Best wishes,\r<br>Ron.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "TOkjI8XWBAAJ",
   "from": "Alchiba",
   "author": "c6f4123be4a725e9",
   "date": "2022-03-16T12:57:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: items desperatly ordered alphabetically with Geom_bar despite stat=identity",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Thanks Ron.<br>I realize effectively that there&#39;s an internal translation of the character x variable as a factor but the levels attributed are not always the ones you want. The solution is to reorder along other levels than the default ones. Once you understand that, it&#39;s simpler to get the correct answer."
    ],
    [
